{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
[Am]Farewell and adieu to you,
[G]Fair Spanish [C]ladies,
[Am]Farewell and adieu to you,
[E]Ladies of [Am]Spain;
For we've [C]received orders
For to [G]sail for old England,
And per[Am]haps we shall never
More [E]see you a[Am]gain.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
We'll [Am]rant and we'll roar
Like [G]true British [C]sailors,
We'll [Am]rant and we'll roar
All [E]on the salt [Am]seas,
Until we [C]strike soundings
In the [G]Channel of old England;
From [Am]Ushant to Scilly
Is [E]thirty-five [Am]leagues.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
We [Am]hove our ship to,
With the [G]wind at sou'-[C]west, boys,
We [Am]hove our ship to
For to [E]strike soundings [Am]clear;
Then we [C]filled the main topsail
And [G]bore right away, boys,
And [Am]straight up the Channel
Our [E]course we did [Am]steer.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
{x_end: Am}
